speechtext:
What was the amount spent by the Department of Immigration and Colonization during the past four years:
(a)	In	promoting	immigration	from	the	British
Isles;
(b)	In	promoting	immigration	from	the	United
States of America;
(c)	In promoting immigration from the continent of Europe ?

For a return showing in detail,-(a) A list of all the parties sent out by the Geological Survey in the year 1923; (b) The names of the Chief of each party;
(c) The District to which each party was assigned;
(d) The names and home addresses of all temporary field assistants; (e) The names of the Universities from which such assistants came; (f) The undergraduate year of each of such assistants; (g) The name and year of graduation and name of each university of each graduate in each party; (h) The special qualifications of each of such assistants; (i) The remuneration and travelling expenses of each.
